cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "kernR: Kernel-Based Causal Distributional Testing"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-04-25
abstract: >
  Kernel-based hypothesis tests for causal inference and distributional
  treatment effects. Implements backdoor-adjusted HSIC (bd-HSIC) for
  testing causal association, and doubly robust kernel statistics
  (DR-DATE, DR-DETT) for testing distributional treatment effects beyond
  mean shifts. Supports binary, continuous, and mixed treatments,
  hierarchical/nested data structures, and scales to larger datasets via
  Nystrom approximation and random Fourier features.
